# GET /setup — fast every call, so the edge never times out on it.
#
# It reports readiness, and if the workspace is not ready it kicks provisioning
# + launch off DETACHED (setsid) and returns immediately; the page POLLS /setup
# until ready, each poll reporting the latest PHASE. This is the
# provisioning-vs-cold-start seam made real: the slow apt install happens out of
# band, not in the HTTP request. `pgrep ws-provision.sh` is the "already
# running" check; readiness is marker==REQ + a chromium binary + x11vnc on 5900.
#
# Each /setup is a real exec, which also WAKES the sprite (it idle-sleeps ~30s
# after the last exec) — the page keep-alive-polls this while VNC is open so the
# display does not freeze. Runtime version + packages are DATA (env).
#
# The script is setup.sh, beside this op: `&include` writes it in as the
# stdin string when txco reads the OPS/ tree, so it stays a plain file.
WHEN @src == "http" && @web.req.url.path == "/setup"
  EXEC "workspace://tools/exec"
    WITH command = "bash -s",
         env     = &object("REQ", "5"),   # runtime version; bump to re-provision
         timeout = "45s",
         into    = "_setup",
         stdin   = &include("setup.sh")
